# Optional -- docker-compose.yml already bundles a Byparr container
# (see its own comment) and defaults FLARESOLVERR_URL to that, so you
# don't need this file at all just to get a working stack. Only set this
# if you'd rather point at a FlareSolverr or Byparr instance running
# elsewhere on your network instead (e.g. one you already run for other
# *arr apps) -- uncomment and fill in below, then docker-compose.yml picks
# it up automatically (read from this same directory).
#
# Byparr: https://github.com/ThePhaseless/Byparr -- solves Cloudflare's
# Turnstile/Managed Challenge (which Forex Factory sits behind as of
# 2026-08) with a real Camoufox browser under the hood. FlareSolverr
# (https://github.com/FlareSolverr/FlareSolverr) speaks the same API and
# works as a drop-in alternative here, but reliably failed to clear Forex
# Factory's current Turnstile challenge in direct testing -- see
# LXC/README.md's own writeup. Either way, calendar_api.py just needs
# something answering this FlareSolverr-compatible /v1 API at this address.
# FLARESOLVERR_URL=http://192.168.1.50:8191
